Single-database configuration for Flask.

Pristine PostgreSQL initialization
----------------------------------

The supported schema bootstrap is the same command used for upgrades::

    AUTO_INIT_ON_STARTUP=false python -m flask db upgrade heads

Do not run ``db.create_all()``, generate migrations during deployment, restore a
schema-only dump, or stamp an empty database.  The committed migration graph
has two expected heads (``5202003d1ec0`` and
``20260812_pop_history``), and CI proves that a pristine PostgreSQL 16
database reaches both heads without startup-time schema mutation.

After the upgrade, run explicit data seed/import operations separately.  In
particular, ``AUTO_INIT_ON_STARTUP=false`` intentionally prevents application
startup from creating tables, columns, indexes, or seed records behind
Alembic's back.

Only forward upgrades are supported for deployment.  Rollback restores a
verified PostgreSQL backup and the previous immutable application release;
``flask db downgrade`` is not a supported production rollback mechanism.
